{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072792-deity-shadow-names-help-please","id":1072792,"title":"Deity Shadow Names help please!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-03T17:15:03-07:00","id":1072792,"title":"Deity Shadow Names help please!","content":"Looking for suggestions for Deity shadow names for several NPCs. Covering every Watchtower, and a good range of real world cultures. I know I could spend some time on Wikipedia for this, but I want to pick the brains of my fellow gamers first. Thanks everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11852-arcane_pozhar","name":"Arcane_Pozhar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T19:33:01-07:00","id":1072883,"title":"","content":"Every concept under the Sun (including the Sun) can be found in lists of god names. Are there any particular concepts you like?<br /> <br /> Also worth mentioning is that Shadow Names really don't have to be deity names. That's an old and common practice, but you can really pick any sort of descriptive title you like and define what it means to your character. &quot;Thousand Yard Stare&quot;, &quot;Cracking Ice&quot;, and &quot;White Moonlight&quot; are all good Shadow Name ideas if you can craft associations and what they mean to your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T20:07:31-07:00","id":1072897,"title":"","content":"Yeah, asking for Shadow Names without character concepts is like asking for book covers without saying what's inside. I like that comparison a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T06:06:18-07:00","id":1073065,"title":"","content":"I agree with WHW that concepts are incredible important. I have a friend who is playing a character who bases all of his shadow names for his character after the irish god Lugh. Starting out a teen mage his character was named <i>Macnia</i> (&quot;youthful warrior/hero&quot;). He changed his shadow name to <i>Ild\u00e1nach</i> (&quot;skilled in many arts&quot;) when he had successfully initiated all 10 Arcana, wants to change his shadow name to <i>Samild\u00e1nach</i> (&quot;equally skilled in many arts&quot;) if he ever successfully apprentices all 10 Arcana, and to <i>Lugh</i> if he ever becomes a disciple of all 10.<br /> <br /> \u200bMany gods have alternate names/epitheths and I would recommend looking into those as well since they are often essentially deed names and provide strong focus for both player and npc characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T06:38:09-07:00","id":1073081,"title":"","content":"I agree with the above, but I'll list some names anyway.<br /> <br /> Norse:<br /> Thor - God of Strength and battle<br /> Odin - God of Wisdom and Death<br /> Frey - God of agriculture and fertility<br /> Heimdall - God of Light and Steadfastness<br /> Freya - God of Beauty and Love<br /> Loki - God of Lies and Fire<br /> Balder - God of Beauty and Light<br /> Njord - God of the Sea<br /> Aegir - (also) God of the Sea (but actually a giant)<br /> Tyr - God of Armies and War<br /> Bragi - God of Poetry and Skjalds<br /> Idun - God of Youth<br /> <br /> Greek<br /> Zeus - God of the Heavens<br /> Hera - God of Wisdom and Women<br /> Athena - God of War and Wisdom<br /> Apollo - God of the Sun and Physical Exploits<br /> Artemis - God the Wilds and Hunts<br /> Ares - God of War<br /> Afrodite - God of Love and Beauty<br /> Hades - God of Death and Wealth<br /> Morpheus - God (?) of Sleep<br /> Hecate - God of Magic<br /> Dionysus - God of Wine and Parties<br /> Vulcan - God of Smiths<br /> Hermes - God of Secrets and Merchants<br /> Poseidon - God of the Sea<br /> <br /> Egyptian<br /> Ra - God of the Sun<br /> Set - God of the Desolate Places<br /> Thoth - God of Wisdom<br /> Osiris - God of Agriculture<br /> Anubis - God of Passage and Death<br /> Bastet - God of Cats and Home<br /> Sobek - God of the Nile<br /> Isis - God of Women and Motherhood<br /> Horus - God of the Sky<br /> Nephthys - God of the Dead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T03:47:40-07:00","id":1074081,"title":"","content":"Also, each god is not just his portfolio. What's the difference between Apollo, Helios and Ra? All deities are associated with Sun, two of them are even from the same pantheon. My point is that it is important not only a defined Player concept but also the knowledge of a Deity's mythos for the Shadowname to have proper depth/symbolism.<br /> <br /> More on the matter, what happens when two Shadownames are linked? What happens between Apollo and Ra? Between Hercules and Hera?<br /> On my games, inspired by years of Dungeons and Dragons, when similar Universal Aspects exist at once (like two Gods of the Sun at the same pantheon) they are destined to collide until they merge or one of them ceases to exist.<br /> <br /> The hierarch of my Setting is named Apollo (a righteous authoritarian figure), one of my players is named Ra (a rebelous liberal assassin). That eventual conflict was straightforward for me to handle (and plan for their eventual &quot;merge&quot;, like their Greek-Egyptian cults counterparts). Other times can be tricky, especially when the NPCs or PCs are not properly fleshed out, or when I have just superficial knowledge of some deities like Heimdall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T07:29:17-07:00","id":1074117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane_Pozhar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072792-deity-shadow-names-help-please#post1072792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking for suggestions for Deity shadow names for several NPCs. Covering every Watchtower, and a good range of real world cultures. I know I could spend some time on Wikipedia for this, but I want to pick the brains of my fellow gamers first. Thanks everyone!</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing immediately popped to mind:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA p.292</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a wise old master tells his students, \u201cDon\u2019t pick Odin for your Shadow Name if you are overly fond of both your eyes.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>This means if the NPCs are smart, clever and wise they won't choose deity names who's story elements are something they wouldn't be okay with.<br /> <br /> Choose Fenris? Be savage, hunger for light, get trapped, be released to the doom of the world (maybe just <i>your </i>world, like your friends and family), plunges the world into darkness after devouring the light, all of which is particularly appropriate themes for a mage's dark story arch.<br /> <br /> Choose Immanuel? Be a great healer and rebuker of the wicked but also be painfully martyred. Someone may still choose this if the idea of self sacrifice resonates with them.<br /> <br /> Choose Loki? Wow, what a wierd masochist are you... Birthing a horse, getting caught in a net, betraying friends because of a relationship, siring monsters, being tortured by former friends. All because you didn't read any of his myths and went with the surface &quot;shapeshifting tricker&quot; label<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 04-06-2017, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T08:04:38-07:00","id":1074658,"title":"","content":"Someone posted this link on the forums a while back which I find helpful <a href=\"http://www.mythologydictionary.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.mythologydictionary.com/</a><br /> <br /> I found it helpful in finding names which felt like they had an occult flavour/deeper meaning, but lacked the sort of hubristic edge that comes with naming yourself after very well known mythological characters like Odin or Loki.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T09:45:16-07:00","id":1074714,"title":"","content":"That'd be me, yo. It is a great link to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T22:18:37-07:00","id":1075001,"title":"","content":"Ra : Sets up rules, so Acanthus could like him, Father of Osiris,The Egyptian God of the Sun<br /> Osiris : Moros, Father of Horus,The Egyptian God of the Sun<br /> Horus : Sorta Thyrsus, Father of Osiris,The Egyptian God of the Sun<br /> Aten : Obrimos,The Egyptian God of the Sun<br /> <br /> <br /> Chernobog: God of the Charred Hamburgers and Burnt Hair; associated with the Mastigos and particularly funky Moros.<br /> Belobog: God of grills, lanterns, and beach parties; associated with Obrimos<br /> <br /> Terminus : God of journeys and crossroads, Mastigos and Thyrsus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T19:43:02-07:00","id":1082876,"title":"","content":"Greetings from the Philippines. We have a plethora of (far more obscure) deities from our indigenous animist traditions. Why not give these a try?<br /> <br /> Bathala - Creator god of the Tagalogs<br /> Idiyanale - Goddess of labor and good deeds<br /> Lakanpati - Fertility god<br /> Aman Sinaya - Goddess of fishermen<br /> Diyan Masalanta - Goddess of love and fertiity<br /> Kabunian - A tribal god of the Igorot ethnic group<br /> Anitong Tawo - God of wind and rain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}